/* Beat 4, composed onto ScreenScaffold. What is left in this file is the
 * three things the frame and the components cannot know: the gap under the
 * prompt, the centring of the one card, and that two of these labels wrap.
 *
 * FOUR RULES LEFT THIS FILE IN PHASE 8 TASK 9 AND NONE OF THEM WERE
 * REPLACED BY A COPY HERE, which is the whole test of whether a screen is
 * composing the layer or re-deriving it:
 *   - the root's `padding: var(--gutter)` is the scaffold's content region.
 *   - `__prompt`'s font-size/colour/weight is `t-section` in the UXML; the
 *     screen TITLE moved to the scaffold's header, so the prompt is no
 *     longer also acting as one.
 *   - `__blocker`'s fill, radius and padding are Theme's `.panel-coral` and
 *     its ink is `.t-danger`.
 *   - `__skip`'s whole treatment was a verbatim second copy of Theme's
 *     `.btn-quiet`, down to the `:active` rule.
 *   - `__confirm` and `__name`'s margins are the CTA row's padding and
 *     Theme's own TextField margin.
 */
.founder-naming-view { flex-grow: 1; }

.founder-naming-view__prompt {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
    white-space: normal;
}

/* The card holds one CreatureCard, which is a fixed 160px tile - so the
 * centring is the container's job and cannot come from the tile. */
.founder-naming-view__founder {
    flex-direction: row;
    justify-content: center;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
}

/* A sentence, not a label, so it wraps. Shown only when it says something -
 * FounderNamingView.Blocker has the measurement. */
.founder-naming-view__blocker {
    white-space: normal;
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
}
